Node ID=100 the ore
Text=<He is quiet for a moment, and it is not the quiet of a creature deciding whether to speak. It is the quiet of one deciding whether you are worth the words.>  Not need. Owed.  <He puts a finger against the rock beside him, and the finger is the size of your forearm.>  There is red ore in this rock. It goes up in a sack on a small man's back, in the night, and nothing comes down. Not food. Not iron. Not one word of asking.  We know where it goes. The smith. Eduardo. We have known that name a long time.  We are not thieves. We do not want to be robbed by them either.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then set a price and I will carry it up myself.
Go to node ID=101 terms given
Icon=Quest Icon

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=The men above will never agree to pay for what they can steal.
Go to node ID=101 terms given

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Not today.
Go to node ID=
Icon=Exit Icon
Is Default Reply=1
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=101 terms given
Text=Then hear it, and carry it whole.  <He counts on those enormous fingers, slowly, so you cannot mistake him.>  We dig. We stack. The smith sends one man, in daylight, and that man knocks on the rock and waits to be answered. He pays iron, not coin -- coin is no good in the dark. And he sends the same man each time, so we know the face.  <He closes his hand.>  That is all of it. It is not much to ask of a man who has been taking it for free.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Iron, daylight, and the same man each time. I will tell him.
