Node ID=130 the man above
Text=Enrique Garcia. The one who keeps the beggars.  <He says the name the way you would say a debt.>  He has been paying for it for a long time. The ones out there on the rock were his, some of them.  <He says this without heat, which is somehow worse.>  We cannot go up and say anything about it. A troll in your streets is a thing that gets a bell rung. So it goes on being paid, and men keep coming down, and we keep putting them on the rock, and none of that is talking.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I can go up. Let me say it for you.
Go to node ID=131 say it then
Icon=Quest Icon
Is Default Reply=1

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=Then it goes on.
Go to node ID=
Icon=Exit Icon
------------------------------------------------------------
Node ID=131 say it then
Text=<He considers this for a while, and you get the distinct sense he is deciding whether it is a kindness or a trick, and that he has been wrong about that before.>  Then say this, and say it in these words. We did not come up. Not once. In all of it, not one of us has ever gone up your stairs.  <He holds up a finger.>  Everything that has happened has happened down here, on our rock, to people who came to it. Ask him what he is paying for. Ask him if he can say the same.
Should Have Voiceover=0

Requirement=!None
Reply Text=I will say exactly that.
